description:
Add verdict delivery after the second resolveFeatureCompose call site in repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts so its execution rows stop being permanently ungraded.

REGION / ANCHOR. Ground on this exact line, which occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file:
  const cb = compose.body as Record<string, unknown>;
Insert the new code on the lines IMMEDIATELY AFTER that single line, before the comment block beginning "CLOSE-ON-LAND: only when the fix GENUINELY landed on origin/dev". Do not modify any other part of the file. Do not touch the top of the file or any import.

ONE OPERATION: insert this block verbatim, unchanged:

  try {
    const reachId2 = typeof cb["execution_id"] === "string" ? (cb["execution_id"] as string) : "";
    if (reachId2.length > 0) {
      const reachEndpoint2 = process.env["METABOB_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8080";
      const reachKey2 = process.env["METABOB_API_KEY"] ?? "";
      void fetch(`${reachEndpoint2}/v2/activities/execution-traces/reach`, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(reachKey2 ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${reachKey2}` } : {}) },
        body: JSON.stringify({ execution_id: reachId2, reached: cb["ok"] === true }),
        signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000),
      }).catch(() => { /* grading must never affect the compose result */ });
    }
  } catch { /* verdict delivery is best effort */ }

WHY THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE. This replicates, at a second call site, a block ALREADY LIVE in this same file: search for the identical block using the variable name reachId (no digit), landed in commit c5468ed and currently deployed. That first block is on the hot path and has been observed delivering verdicts (HTTP 200 at the receiver). This file calls resolveFeatureCompose at three sites; only the first delivers a reach verdict, so composes that take this second path write execution rows that no arm ever learns from. The fetch is deliberately fire-and-forget so grading can never affect the compose result -- that is the established pattern here, not a stub.

